+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registered on `ToolRegistry` in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` (`src/types/ai.ts`) that is forwarded to the AI provider. `ToolRegistry.execute` validates incoming `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor, returning a `ToolResponse` describing the failure on schema violations so the model can correct its call within the orchestrator's tool-round budget rather than aborting the conversation, while throwing only when the tool name itself is unregistered.
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once during `register`, throwing an error that names the tool when the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws at registration time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L13)).
+- A static tool reuses its compiled validator across repeated `execute` calls rather than recompiling the schema on each call.
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned on that call, caching compiled validators by schema object identity rather than holding a stale schema from an earlier call ([validated by: validates a function-valued tool definition against the schema returned on each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L77)).
+
+## Execution contract and value redaction
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` enforces `required`, declared property types, and `enum` constraints without coercing values, applying defaults, or injecting `additionalProperties: false`, and when input violates the schema it skips the executor and returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing property path and expected constraint while omitting both the offending value and every other input field value from the returned text and from log output ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming the path and expected type without calling the executor or leaking input values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L28)).
+- When `ChatOrchestrator` in `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` executes a rejected tool call, the returned `ToolResponse.result` is sent back to the provider as a `tool_result` message instead of throwing, allowing the model to retry within the round limit and passing valid input — including unlisted extra properties — unchanged to the executor ([validated by: returns a missing-required-field rejection to the model so a retry with extra properties succeeds](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L114)).
+- Valid input with unlisted extra properties is passed through to the executor unchanged, without adding defaults or coercing values, and invokes the executor once.
+- Calling `ToolRegistry.execute` with an unregistered tool name throws `Unknown tool: <name>`, preserving the failure contract for unknown tools.
